{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>So that his heart not be exalted.</b> The explanation follows the way of our Sages of blessed memory (Avot 6:1): ״וּמַלְבַּשְׁתּוֹ עֲנָוָה וְיִרְאָה״ — 'and clothe him in humility and fear.' And this is what it means: through the regular reading of the Torah his heart will not be exalted, etc. And corresponding to the fear it said just before this: ״לְמַעַן יִלְמַד לְיִרְאָה״ — 'so that he learns to fear.'"], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:17:54.794211096Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}